      "name": "double-transfer-form",
      "axis": "fp-double-transfer",
      "what_it_counts": "double-width memory transfers, by whether one access or two carries the value",
      "discriminating": false,
      "non_discriminating": "ldc1 and sdc1 move 64 bits in one access under either register file: with a 32-bit file the access writes the even/odd pair, with a 64-bit file it writes one register. Their presence dates the instruction set at MIPS II or later and says nothing about register width, and every N64 target is MIPS III, so the count separates no two toolchains in this corpus. It is carried because the shape is worth counting and dropping it would leave the earlier reading of it unanswered.",
